# OmGold ERP — reverse proxy.
#
# REMOVED, deliberately: a `@transform_port_query` matcher that did
#     reverse_proxy localhost:{query.XTransformPort}
# It let ANY visitor choose the upstream port from the query string. `?XTransformPort=3306`
# reached MySQL; any other local service was one number away. The app's login was not bypassed
# so much as skipped — the request never reached the app at all. Nothing in this repo used it,
# and there is no safe way to keep a visitor-chosen upstream: the value cannot be validated into
# safety, because every port worth protecting is a port someone could type.
#
# The default upstream also pointed at 3000 while the app serves 3002, so this file could not
# have worked as written.
:81 {
	handle {
		reverse_proxy localhost:3002 {
			header_up Host {host}
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
			header_up X-Forwarded-Proto {scheme}
			header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
		}
	}
}
